For starters, when facing a Titan, *always* retain the option of going
back up the stairs.  If you are tempted for any reason to step off the
stairs, don't, unless you have some other reliable way of going back
up (e.g., cursed potion of gain level) in your main inventory.  Even
then, be careful, because if some kind of heat or cold attack destroys
your way out you can find yourself in serious trouble real fast, and
you may not have a spare turn to delve into your bag for another.
Honestly, I think not leaving the up stair is really the best approach
when there's a Titan afoot.

Also, it would be a good idea to have both reflection and magic
resistance before attempting to do battle with a Titan.  (You said you
had Magicbane, but you also implied you weren't wielding it.  Did you
have another source of MR?)

Also, watch your hitpoints and leave early, before you're mostly dead,
and save enough power to teleport at least once afterward.  Some of
the things Titans summon will follow you up the stairs, so you may
take several palpable hits the turn after you go up, and then you'll
need to get away and heal.  Going up and then teleporting to the
former up stairs and going up again can buy you a chance to get some
of your hitpoints back.

Titans are more dangerous than most of the monsters in Gehennom (I
believe everything nastier is either a named unique monster or a
popular genocide target, e.g., purple L).  Facing a Titan is a major
serious big deal NOT to be undertaken lightly, especially pre-castle.


